***
***	<comment from="gemini-3-flash-preview">
***	The original Maude code is simplified and improved for efficiency by adopting the sort structure and operator overloading conventions from the standard Maude `LIST` module (Section 8.14.1 of the manual). Specifically, I introduced the `NeList` sort to represent non-empty lists and overloaded the concatenation operator `__`. This refined sort structure allows the Maude engine to perform sort calculation more efficiently and avoids unnecessary associative searching. The `length` function remains linear, and by specifying the head of the list as the `Letter` sort (the atom sort), the associative matcher can efficiently decompose the list into a single element and the remainder in O(1) time per step.
***	</comment>
***

fmod SIMPLE-LIST is
  protecting NAT .
  sorts Letter NeList List .
  subsort Letter < NeList < List .
  ops a b c d : -> Letter [ctor] .
  op nil : -> List [ctor] .
  op __ : List List -> List [ctor assoc id: nil prec 25] .
  op __ : NeList List -> NeList [ctor ditto] .
  op __ : List NeList -> NeList [ctor ditto] .
  op length : List -> Nat .
  var E : Letter .
  var L : List .
  eq length(nil) = 0 .
  eq length(E L) = s length(L) .
endfm